>
>> 4) Healer - Grayswandir
>
>Upgrading from the Staff of Aesculapius to Grayswandir is about as
>helpful as wishing for "nothing" in the late game.  Pre-quest, an elven
>short sword and an athame is usually more than enough offense.

  The staff is twohanded and a plain quarterstaff vs level-drain 
resistant monsters.  There are a lot of level drain resistant monsters 
in Gehennom and beyond.  Twohandedness is a deathtrap when cursed 
in Gehennom.  Twohanded means no shield: 6-9 fewer AC.  The staff 
can still be #invoked even if not wielded.  

  The Wizard of Yendor will also try to steal it.


  What monsters are level drain resistant?  undead, demons, 
were-creatures, and Death.  Undead include ghosts, shades, and
all LMVWZ.


  Without the level drain attack the quarterstaff does just 3.5 base 
damage to all monsters, large or small.  (Ask a starting wizard how 
bad that is.)

